{
  "subject": "fix: give the morphing modal dialog semantics, Escape and focus hand-back",
  "capturedAt": "2026-09-21T11:47:41.356Z",
  "page": "/components/motion/morphing-modal",
  "trigger": "Open wallet options",
  "defect": "The morphing modal rendered a plain <div> panel: no role=\"dialog\", no aria-modal, no accessible name, no Escape handler and no focus management. Escape did nothing, and closing it left document.activeElement on <body> in both browsers.",
  "method": "Per browser and build, two paths. Mouse: click the trigger with no prior focus call. Keyboard: focus the trigger with window.__audit.focusAt() and press Enter. While open, record whether an element with role=\"dialog\" and aria-modal=\"true\" is present, its aria-label, and document.activeElement. Then press Escape and poll every 100 ms for up to 1200 ms for the panel disappearing or going pointer-events: none. If Escape does nothing, close with the demo's own close control (aria-label \"Close\"). Finally record document.activeElement again.",
  "environment": {
    "machine": "macOS 26.6.2",
    "chrome": {
      "version": "153.0.8010.50",
      "driver": "Playwright, chromium.launch({ channel: \"chrome\", headless: false })",
      "viewport": "1440x900"
    },
    "safari": {
      "version": "26.6.2",
      "driver": "safaridriver (W3C WebDriver) on port 4491",
      "viewport": "1440x900"
    }
  },
  "builds": {
    "before": {
      "label": "upstream main",
      "origin": "http://localhost:3300",
      "servedFrom": "wt/upstream-main"
